Generated Structured Text logic for Schneider M340 devices now supports I/O variables of every IEC 61131-3 type that can be located. Each gets an address whose size matches the type (``%QX`` for BOOL, ``%QB`` for 8-bit, ``%MW`` for 16-bit, ``%MD`` for 32-bit and ``%ML`` for 64-bit types), which OpenPLC v3 and v4 map to I/O and memory. Previously only INT and BOOL I/O variables were supported.
I/O variables that can't be located (ARRAY, STRING, TIME and the date types) are now declared without an address instead of being skipped, and STRING variables now generate valid TC6 XML.
